    "updated_at": "2022-09-09T14:55:51Z",
    "body": "The steps are:\r\n\r\n1. Initiate a pairing with `requestDevice({ filter })`, user selects from dialog an un-paired device, call `open()` on device\r\n2. Call `forget( )` on device and clear reference to device\r\n3. Re-initiate a pairing with `requestDevice({filter})`, select same un-paired device, call `open( )` on device -- returns error on open call indicating the \"device is forgotten\".  Any other calls on the device return an error.\r\n4. Re-fresh the browser, call `getDevice()` and device is returned as a paired device\r\n\r\nI guess my question is: is there any way to re-pair a forgotten device without requiring a browser refresh?  I'm trying to build in a robust pair/forget algorithm for the devices we are using.  Two things were unexpected behavior: 1. once the device is forgotten, it seems there is no way to recover and re-pair without refresh 2. step 4 above I was surprised to see the device returned as paired after the error and refresh.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
